  "architecture_name": "[efficientnet_b0] effnet_b0_mixup_heavy_aug",
  "architecture_family": "efficientnet_b0",
  "description": "EfficientNet-B0 with ImageNet pretrained weights, 1\u21923 channel expansion via conv1x1, input resized to 224x224, classifier head replaced with Dropout(0.3)\u2192Linear(1280,206) with sigmoid, trained with mixup (alpha=0.5) and SpecAugment (freq_mask=20, time_mask=40) to handle long-tail classes.",
  "reasoning": "As the first experiment, EfficientNet-B0 is the strongest pretrained backbone available in the registry and typically outperforms ResNet18 on mel-spectrogram tasks. It's still small enough (~5.3M params) for CPU inference within the 90-minute budget. Pretrained features transfer well to audio spectrograms. Heavy augmentation (mixup + SpecAugment) should help with the long-tail distribution by improving generalization on minority classes. This establishes a strong baseline to iterate from."
}
